      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, i manage a rental property in phoenix and one of the tenants is complaining that their central AC is running constantly but one of the bedrooms stays really warm. any idea what might be causing uneven cooling like that?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Uneven cooling in one room usually points to an issue with airflow distribution or system balance. The ductwork leading to that bedroom might be partially blocked, damaged, or improperly sealed, restricting cold air from reaching it. Alternatively, the thermostat might be located in a different area and not accurately sensing the temperature in the warm room.",
